\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Must every syntactically homogeneous depth-five $\Sigma \Pi \Sigma \Pi \Sigma $ circuit over C computing the (1,1) entry of a product of n independent n×n variable matrices have size at least $n^{c\surd n}$ for some $c>0$ and all sufficiently large n?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Must every syntactically homogeneous depth-five $\Sigma \Pi \Sigma \Pi \Sigma $ circuit over C computing the (1,1) entry of a product of n independent n×n variable matrices have size at least $n^{c\surd n}$ for some $c>0$ and all sufficiently large n?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://eccc.weizmann.ac.il/report/2021/023/download/}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
